From 5cd6c5c082063c2236096e455964c440b28bcc9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:27:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ship libimagequant's licence alongside imagequant's own

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; the same gap exists in every imagequant wheel on PyPI, so this needs a maintainer discussion rather than a drive-by PR]

The extension statically compiles the bundled libimagequant C sources
(libimagequant/*.c, built in-process by imagequant/libimagequant_build.py's
cffi ffibuilder.set_source()), which carry their own notice: BSD-style for
the original pngquant code plus GPL v3-or-later for Kornel Lesinski's
additions (libimagequant/COPYRIGHT). setup.py declares no [metadata]
license_files, so setuptools' default LICEN[CS]E* glob only picks up
imagequant's own BSD-3-Clause LICENSE, and the built wheel ships a single
notice covering the wrapper alone.

Adding an explicit license_files list (there is no tracked setup.cfg to
extend) names the vendored file in place, so the patch tracks the submodule
and setuptools preserves its path relative to the project root: it lands in
the wheel as dist-info/licenses/libimagequant/COPYRIGHT.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 setup.cfg | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 setup.cfg

diff --git a/setup.cfg b/setup.cfg
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7379387
--- /dev/null
+++ b/setup.cfg
@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@
+[metadata]
+license_files =
+    LICENSE
+    libimagequant/COPYRIGHT
-- 
2.43.0

